# Logging & Observability

Structured logs for every job step, so a failure can be diagnosed from CloudWatch alone.

## Log Format

```
2026-11-26T16:00:03 INFO    JOB START fetch-daily
2026-11-26T16:00:04 INFO    fetch: start ET 2026-11-27
2026-11-26T16:00:04 INFO    fetch: A got 11 games from schedule
2026-11-26T16:00:12 INFO    fetch: D matched 11 of 11 games, 0 unmatched
2026-11-26T16:00:12 INFO    fetch: G window stored: 2026-11-27T23:20:00+00:00 -> 2026-11-28T04:00:00+00:00 (11 games)
2026-11-26T16:00:12 INFO    JOB END fetch-daily ok
```

Each line is `timestamp | level | message`. The message carries the job and the
step, because CloudWatch merges the whole stdout stream into one blob - a
banner or a multi-line message turns into an unreadable paragraph. **One
line per event, no banners.**

## Naming Conventions

| Prefix | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `JOB START <name>` | Handler entry |
| `JOB END <name> ok` | Handler exited successfully |
| `fetch: <letter> ...` | A step of the daily fetch (A-I) |
| `scale: ...` | A step of the scale job |
| `trade-worker: ...` | A step of the SQS worker |
| `snapshot-price: ...` | A step of the snapshot job |
| `dashboard-api: ...` | A step of the dashboard API |
| `WARNING` | Something degraded but the job continued |
| `ERROR` | The step failed; the exception follows |

## The Daily Fetch Steps

| Letter | Action | What a healthy line looks like |
|--------|--------|-------------------------------|
| A | NBA schedule from API Ninjas | `fetch: A got 11 games from schedule` |
| B | Standings | `fetch: B got standings for 30 teams` |
| C | Polymarket Gamma events | `fetch: C got 57 Polymarket events` |
| D | Match schedule to events | `fetch: D matched 11 of 11 games, 0 unmatched` |
| E | Write game metadata | `fetch: E wrote 11 game metadata items` |
| F | Write daily batch | `fetch: F daily batch written` |
| G | Compute + store listener window | `fetch: G window stored: <start> -> <end> (11 games)` |
| H | Create one-shot window schedules | `fetch: H window scale schedules done` |
| I | Telegram notification | `fetch: I Telegram notification sent` |

### What to check when something looks wrong

| Symptom | Root cause | Fix |
|---------|-----------|-----|
| `fetch: A got 0 games` | API Ninjas has no games for that ET date | Rest day, or the date is wrong. Check the ET date the job resolved. |
| `fetch: D matched 0 of N` | Schedule matcher failed, or Gamma has no matching market | Check `fetch: C` count - if it is 0, Gamma is down; if it is large, the matcher is at fault. |
| `fetch: G no listener window` | No matched games, so no tip-offs to derive the window from | The listener will not auto-scale. The scale-up backstop covers it. |
| `fetch: H` says no `SCHEDULER_ROLE_ARN` | `FetchDailyFunction` is missing the env var | The template must set `SCHEDULER_ROLE_ARN` on the fetch function. |
| `scale: no window (no games, or fetch has not run yet)` | The daily fetch has not written games for today | Check the fetch logs. |
| `scale: current desired count=None` | ECS call failed or the service does not exist | Check the deploy and the `LambdaRole` IAM grant. |
| `trade-worker: message ... FAILED` | Malformed SQS message or stale game state | The message is redriven; check the exception detail. |
| `dashboard-api: FAILED building dashboard` | DynamoDB query failed | Check the GSI1 IAM grant on `LambdaRole`. |

## Checking Logs

### In the console

CloudWatch -> Log groups -> `ap-east-1` -> `/aws/lambda/polymarket-sports-*`.

Useful filter patterns:

| Pattern | Finds |
|---------|-------|
| `ERROR` | Failed steps, with the traceback |
| `"JOB START"` | Every invocation of every job |
| `"JOB END"` | Invocations that finished cleanly |
| `"fetch: G"` | The listener window for each day |
| `"scale:"` | The scale decisions every 5 minutes |

### From the CLI

```bash
# Tail the daily fetch
aws logs tail /aws/lambda/polymarket-sports-fetch-daily --follow --region ap-east-1

# Errors in the last 2 hours
aws logs filter-log-events \
  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/polymarket-sports-fetch-daily \
  --filter-pattern "ERROR" \
  --start-time $(( $(date +%s) - 7200 ))000 \
  --region ap-east-1
```

## Adding Logs to New Code

One line per event. No banners, no multi-line messages.

```python
logger.info("myjob: doing the thing")
try:
    result = do_thing()
    logger.info("myjob: thing done, got %d items", len(result))
except Exception as e:
    logger.error("myjob: thing FAILED: %s", e, exc_info=True)
    raise
```

Use `%s` lazy formatting rather than f-strings, so the message is only
rendered if the level is enabled.

## Notes

- The Lambda runtime already installs a root handler that writes to stdout,
  so `configure_logging` only has to set the level and the format.
- `exc_info=True` on every error line: the traceback is what actually
  identifies the fault, and it costs nothing when there is no error.
- Steps that can fail but are allowed to fail (the Telegram notification,
  the window schedules) log at WARNING and do not raise.
